# What does not go into a built copy of this plugin.
#
# WHO READS THIS FILE, AND WHY IT IS NOT .gitattributes
# -----------------------------------------------------
# .gitattributes already carries `export-ignore` on docs/ and tests/, and that
# is honoured by `git archive` and by nothing else. A WordPress.org build is
# not a git archive: the directory is served from SVN, and the zip is made by
# copying a checkout — by `wp dist-archive`, or by the deploy action most
# repositories use, both of which read this file and neither of which reads
# .gitattributes. The two files overlap on purpose and neither replaces the
# other.
#
# HOW THE PATTERNS ARE MATCHED, WHICH IS THE ONE TRAP HERE
# --------------------------------------------------------
# The deploy action hands this file to `rsync --exclude-from`, where a pattern
# with no slash in it matches a name at ANY depth. `README.md` on its own would
# therefore also exclude assets/leaflet/README.md and
# assets/markercluster/README.md — the two files that record where the bundled
# libraries came from and what their SHA-512 digests are, which is exactly the
# evidence a reviewer asks for.
#
# So anything whose name appears more than once in this repository is anchored
# with a leading slash. A tool that does not understand the anchor matches
# nothing and ships the file, which is the harmless direction to be wrong in.
#
# WHAT MUST NEVER BE ADDED HERE
# -----------------------------
# assets/ in any form. It holds the stylesheets, the scripts, Leaflet,
# Leaflet.markercluster and the marker images, all of which are loaded at
# runtime, and leaflet.css references images/ by relative path. Excluding any
# of it produces a plugin that installs and then draws a grey box.

# The prose about how this plugin was built, rather than about how to use it.
docs

# The suite. It calls shell_exec(), tempnam(), file_put_contents(), unlink()
# and set_error_handler() — all correct where they are, none of it anything a
# plugin directory should be asked to host.
tests

# The repository's own front page and its git plumbing. Anchored: README.md is
# also the name of the two provenance files under assets/, which ship.
/README.md
/.distignore
/.gitattributes
/.gitignore
/.git
/.github

# Build tooling, none of which exists today. This plugin has no dependencies
# and no build step; the day one of these arrives, the zip must not grow it.
/composer.json
/composer.lock
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/phpcs.xml
/phpcs.xml.dist
/phpunit.xml
/phpunit.xml.dist
/node_modules
/vendor

# Debris.
*.zip
*.bak
*.bak.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
